module WidgetHandle is
    """
    U13 — the module's side of an owned Rust value.

    `Widget` is a linear record over the two 64-bit words a generated
    `__new` wrapper writes (`owner << 32 | slot`, `provider generation << 32 |
    slot generation`). Only the interface is exported, so a client module
    cannot construct a record itself: `adopt` is the construction seam (it
    takes the words a granted `<target>__new` call produced) and `dispose` is
    the only consumer. That is what makes "destroy it exactly once" a type
    obligation rather than a comment: forgetting a `Widget` is a linearity
    error, and disposing it twice is a use-after-consume error.

    The words are not a value: nothing here dereferences them. `dispose` hands
    them back to the provider's `__dispose` wrapper, which refuses a null pair,
    another registry's owner, a previous provider generation and a stale slot.
    The provider frees its own allocation; neither the module nor the host
    allocator ever does.
    """
    type Widget: Linear;

    -- The construction seam. The words must come from a granted `__new` call;
    -- `dispose` is what turns them back into a refusal or a destructor call.
    function adopt(lo: Int64, hi: Int64): Widget;

    -- The reading seam: borrows the handle (the record stays the module's) and
    -- returns the provider's word, or `-1` when the words were refused — the
    -- slot is not live in this build's registry, so nothing was read.
    generic [R: Region]
    function read(widget: &[Widget, R]): Int64;

    -- The dispose path: destructures the linear record (the obligation is
    -- discharged there) and returns the wrapper's status word — 0 done,
    -- non-zero refused.
    function dispose(widget: Widget): Int64;

    -- The intended path, as a compile-checked witness: mint through a granted
    -- `<target>__new` call, adopt once, read once, dispose once, and return
    -- what the provider said. A second dispose or a forgotten one does not fit
    -- these lines, which is the point of the type.
    function main(): ExitCode;
end module.
